+| D-037 | 2026-09-30 | delivery-orchestrator | **Round-20 repairs: the DG0 gate could not pass on this branch's real history; the pruned-commit tolerance is completed and the delivery metadata corrected (qa's dry-run findings F-DG0-242/243 High, 244 Medium, 241 Low; F-DG0-157 Low).**
• **What qa found.** Round-20 qa drafted a schema-valid APPROVED gate on the frozen candidate and ran `validateGate` on a fresh clone (the auditor's real check) — which `validate.mjs --stage DG0` had never reached because DG0 had no gate record. It reported ~263 errors, most of them permanent gate blockers from the pre-existing history damage that D-035 only partly addressed.
• **F-DG0-242 (High): complete the pruned-commit tolerance.** D-035 tolerated a genuinely-missing commit only in `findManifest`; `checkClosure` (a CLOSED_VERIFIED finding's `fix_revision` must be an ancestor of the round/gate `source_commit`) and `checkInvocation` (a run's `head_commit_at_start` must contain the manifest) still hard-failed on pruned commits — 132 + 63 errors, because 66 closures' `fix_revision`s and 63 runs' `head_commit_at_start`s were truncated (pre-round-12) or rewritten (D-034). Both now tolerate a **genuinely absent** commit (new `commitPresent()` helper, `git cat-file -e <sha>^{commit}`) while still running the check whenever the commit **is** present, so a reachable fix that is not in the candidate, or a run that started before the manifest, is still caught. Same principle and safety as D-035. Test: validator.test.mjs "D-037 / F-DG0-242 …" (present-but-not-in-candidate → still caught; pruned → tolerated; short/non-hex → still rejected).
  Two closures the dry-run then surfaced were **present-but-off-branch**, not absent, so the tolerance rightly did **not** hide them: F-DG0-150/151's `fix_revision` still named `cb76260…`, the **pre**-D-034-rewrite round-17 repair commit (kept alive only by the `backup/pre-writeonce-repair-*` branch), which is not an ancestor of HEAD. The D-034 rewrite re-committed that same repair as `421c922…` (byte-identical `agent_sandbox.py`, an ancestor of HEAD), so per this finding's option (b) their `fix_revision` was **re-pointed to the retained commit** `421c922…` — a metadata correction (identical fix content), leaving them CLOSED_VERIFIED.
• **F-DG0-243 (High): the D-034-kept record-less sidecars no longer block.** The round-17/18 `qa-verifier.{findings,verifications}.json` (kept by D-034 because deleting committed review files violates write-once) each tripped "record … not listed in review_rounds", and F-DG0-238 (raised in the round-17 qa findings sidecar, never imported) was reported "dropped". `collectVerifications` and `collectRaisedFindings` now **skip a sidecar whose own `<role>.json` record file does not exist on disk** — the signature of an interrupted run whose verdict record was never written — while a sidecar whose record file exists but is unlisted is still an error. import-findings already never imported those record-less **verifications**, so nothing in `findings.json` depends on them. **Findings** sidecars are handled to match import-findings exactly (which imports a findings sidecar's findings with or without a record): `collectRaisedFindings` still processes a record-less findings sidecar (so a finding that WAS imported and later closed, e.g. F-DG0-239 raised in the interrupted round-18 qa run and verified in round 19, is not falsely reported "no reviewer sidecar raised it"), but a finding raised **only** by a record-less sidecar and absent from `findings.json` is not a "dropped" finding (`recordless` flag → checkFindings skips the drop error) — it was simply never imported, exactly as import-findings left it. So F-DG0-238 (record-less round-17 sidecar, a duplicate of CLOSED_VERIFIED F-DG0-150, never imported) raises no error, and every finding that IS in `findings.json` still requires a raising sidecar. Test: validator.test.mjs "D-037 / F-DG0-243 …" (record-less verifications and findings sidecars tolerated; once a `<role>.json` record exists the inconsistency is caught again); the real-repo dry-run confirms F-DG0-238/239 clear.
• **F-DG0-244 (Medium): delivery-metadata gaps corrected (no candidate change to these).** The round-19 reviewers' shell test evidence was committed (it had been left untracked, so the verification evidence of F-DG0-152/236/237/239 was absent from clones). Every CLOSED_VERIFIED finding now carries a **full** 40-hex `fix_revision`: F-DG0-152/153 → `1a99d13e…`, F-DG0-239 → `38ffd1da…`, F-DG0-154/155/156/240 → `4008588a…`, and F-DG0-232 (previously null) → `f764edf…` (its AN-11 register fix, a reachable ancestor).
• **F-DG0-241 (Low): gate `source_commit` must be a branch-reachable commit object.** The D-036 check used `git cat-file -e`, which also resolves an off-branch commit or an annotated tag that peels to the frozen commit (QA20-S7, QA20-S8). It now requires the object type to be exactly `commit` (`git cat-file -t`, new `objectType()` helper) **and** an ancestor of HEAD (`isAncestor`) — note `merge-base --is-ancestor` peels a tag, so the type check is what rejects the annotated-tag id, and the ancestry check is what rejects the off-branch commit (which passes locally but is absent from every fresh clone). A missing commit fails the type check. Tests: validator.test.mjs "D-037 / F-DG0-241 …" (off-branch commit and annotated tag) plus the retained D-036 missing-commit test.
• **F-DG0-157 (Low, accepted in round 20): leftover wording fixed.** The `agent_sandbox.py` comment and threat-model residual 7's D-033 credit were corrected to the host-global framing (a host-global `/proc/sys` write has no cross-run *amplification* distinct from the own-process write). | Found in round 20 by qa (real-repo dry-run gate, `docs/delivery/test-evidence/DG0/qa/tests/real-repo-gate-blockers.mjs`). All errors were fail-closed (nothing wrongly approved). **Evidence:** the dry-run categorisation; the new validator behaviour; the round-21 pre-freeze and a clean dry-run gate. | If a later check needs a pruned commit's tree, it cannot be recovered; the tolerances keep content-integrity checks (manifest entries ↔ candidate_id, review binding, findings resolution) and only relax the provenance re-checks that require the vanished commit. |
